findings.body:
In `NavigationException_InAsyncContext_DoesNotBecomeUnobservedTaskException`, `AppContext.SetSwitch("...DisableThrowNavigationException", ...)` changed from `false` to `true`. The test name and its purpose describe the throw path: a NavigationException thrown from an async context must not become an unobserved task exception. With the switch set to `true`, NavigationManager stops throwing that exception, so the code path the test is named for is not exercised.

The test is also quarantined and, because of the MSTest attribute, is never run by xUnit. So this change has no effect on CI today. Once the attribute is fixed and the test runs again, it will pass without testing the scenario it names. The PR should confirm the intended value, or add a comment explaining why the throw path is excluded. The quarantine link (`pull/63708`) should also be checked against this change.

